    <chapter title="Test Scenarios">
        <procedure title="Edits a Case Suspicion Levels Risk Point" id="test-1">
            <p><b>Scenario:</b> Edit and Revert Risk Point</p>
            <p>Updates the first case suspicion level risk point to a new value and then reverts it to the original.</p>
            <step>1. Navigate to Settings → Case Suspicion Levels Risk Points. 2. Click the Edit icon for the first row. 3. Change the risk point value to 2 and save. 4. Verify the success message appears. 5. Click Edit again for the same row. 6. Change the risk point value back to 0 and save. 7. Verify the success message appears again.</step>
            <chapter title="Expected Results">
                <p>• The risk point value is successfully updated both times and the correct success message is displayed.</p>
            </chapter>
        </procedure>
    </chapter>

